From 0b9f3cbd147bccede7c9874558d947951067e903 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:36:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 262/403] Unified: files in and out by purpose
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- After a 2D drawing (DXF, DWG, JWW) is opened, a band under the tool strip
  says what can be done with it: extrude it to a solid (its closed outline
  becomes a part), make a sketch of it, save it as another format. After a
  mesh (STL…): check and fix, make a solid, export for 3D printing.
- ☰ › Import, export, print: for 3D printing (3MF or STL; the fineness, the
  check of the mesh — holes, inside-out faces, edges of more than two faces,
  separate pieces — and "Fix, then export" in one window), to other CAD
  (STEP), 2D (the drawing as DXF or PDF, made first if there is none), an
  image, and any format.
Tested without the GUI: FreeCADCmd -t TestUnifiedFiles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
